---
system: sys-20-content-authoring-review
flow_id: publish-to-system06
surface: internal-RPC
spec_anchor: /software/systems/20-content-authoring-review#scheduling-and-publishing
actors: [AuthoringConsole, AuthoringService, PostgreSQL, SQS, PublishOrchestrator, S3, ContentService]
apis:
  - POST /internal/v1/authoring/schedules
  - POST /internal/v1/authoring/schedules/:id/publish-now
  - POST /internal/v1/authoring/schedules/:id/cancel
externals: [SQS, S3]
queues:
  - ca-publish-execute
  - ca-publish-execute-dlq
failure_paths:
  - schedule_role_insufficient
  - templates_not_approved
  - s3_upload_failure
  - content_service_rejection
  - dlq_after_3_retries
idempotency: pack assembled with content-addressable hash; sys-06 dedup on pack_id
retry: SQS 3 retries with backoff; DLQ on exhaust
timeout: 120s per publish-execute job
status: final
---
%% HAND-CURATED. sys-20 has zero seed — composed from spec §7 publish pipeline + sys-06 hand-off.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant AuthoringConsole
    participant AuthoringService
    participant PostgreSQL
    participant SQS as SQS ca-publish-execute
    participant PublishOrchestrator
    participant S3
    participant ContentService as ContentService (sys-06)

    AuthoringConsole->>AuthoringService: POST /internal/v1/authoring/schedules {template_ids[], scheduled_at, target_pack}

    alt schedule_role_insufficient
        Note over AuthoringService: requires content_admin
        AuthoringService-->>AuthoringConsole: 403 insufficient_role
    else accepted
        AuthoringService->>PostgreSQL: SELECT status FROM ca_authoring_templates WHERE id = ANY($1)
        alt templates_not_approved
            Note over AuthoringService: any template not in 'approved' state
            AuthoringService-->>AuthoringConsole: 422 templates_not_approved
        else all_approved
            AuthoringService->>PostgreSQL: INSERT ca_publish_schedules (template_ids, scheduled_at, status='pending')
            AuthoringService-->>AuthoringConsole: 201 {schedule_id}

            alt publish_now
                AuthoringConsole->>AuthoringService: POST /internal/v1/authoring/schedules/:id/publish-now
                AuthoringService->>SQS: enqueue ca-publish-execute {schedule_id}
            else timer_fires
                Note over SQS: scheduled_at reached → enqueue ca-publish-execute
            else cancelled
                AuthoringConsole->>AuthoringService: POST /internal/v1/authoring/schedules/:id/cancel
                AuthoringService->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE schedule SET status='cancelled'
                Note over SQS: nothing to enqueue
            end

            SQS->>PublishOrchestrator: deliver (timeout 120s)
            PublishOrchestrator->>PostgreSQL: SELECT templates and revalidate status='approved'
            PublishOrchestrator->>PublishOrchestrator: assemble content pack (manifest and template payloads)

            alt s3_upload_failure
                PublishOrchestrator->>S3: PUT content-packs/{pack_id}.json
                S3-->>PublishOrchestrator: error
                PublishOrchestrator--xSQS: NACK (retry)
            else uploaded
                S3-->>PublishOrchestrator: ok
                alt content_service_rejection
                    PublishOrchestrator->>ContentService: publish content pack {pack_id, s3_url, template_ids}
                    ContentService-->>PublishOrchestrator: 422 schema_mismatch
                    PublishOrchestrator->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE schedule SET status='failed', error
                    PublishOrchestrator-->>SQS: ACK (no retry — schema requires author fix)
                else accepted
                    ContentService-->>PublishOrchestrator: 200 published
                    PublishOrchestrator->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE ca_authoring_templates SET status='published', published_at
                    PublishOrchestrator->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE schedule SET status='published'
                    PublishOrchestrator-->>SQS: ACK
                end
            end

            alt dlq_after_3_retries
                SQS--xSQS: 3 retries exhausted → ca-publish-execute-dlq
                Note over SQS: PagerDuty alert
            end
        end
    end

    Note over AuthoringConsole,ContentService: pack-level publish is atomic from sys-06 view — partial template publish never reaches devices — rollback retires pack
